  "_comment": "Enemy forces per front. siege: how hard a unit batters walls (walls.json); escalade: how many men a climbing engine (ladders, siege towers) carries over the walls a round, setupFactor how long it takes to build (x the front's siegeCraft); engine: what the front builds on site to breach them, siegeCraft how long that takes (0: never). Units come in tiers like the player's troops: each front has an infantry, an archer and a cavalry unit in each of four tiers, and a tier joins the hordes from wave index `tiers.minWave` (tier 1 first). weight sets how common a unit is in a wave; each tier unlocked after a unit's own multiplies its weight by `tiers.fade`, so later hordes are mostly the newest troops. Units with no tier (siege engines) keep their own minWave. minPlayers is the smallest group that sees a unit. speed is hexes per hour on plains, like player units. family drives counters in battle; stances weights how often a wave of this front takes each battle stance. personality: lootFactor scales what a raid carries off, raidReach is how far from its road a horde burns outposts, nerve scales its stance's retreat threshold (higher holds longer, capped at never breaking before 95%). razeBias and erratic feed the horde AI (data/horde.json).",
